<section class="section">
	<div class="wrap">
		<p class="eyebrow">Profiles</p>
		<h2>You decide how much it writes for you.</h2>
		<div class="profiles">
			<div><h3>Reader</h3><p>Explains each step. Reading notes are quotes with page numbers and a question for you under each quote. No summaries.</p></div>
			<div><h3>Scholar</h3><p>The default. Literature notes, syntheses, literature reviews and the full librarian. No text for your manuscripts.</p></div>
			<div><h3>Author</h3><p>Scholar, plus help with your manuscripts: citation checks, a bibliography, comments on the argument, reviews against reporting guidelines.</p></div>
			<div><h3>Editor</h3><p>Everything. When you ask, it drafts text for a manuscript and marks the drafted text so that you can check it.</p></div>
		</div>
		<p class="more"><a href="/profiles/">Compare the profiles</a></p>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
	<div class="wrap split">
		<div>
			<p class="eyebrow">What you need</p>
			<h2>Three things. The installer does the rest.</h2>
		</div>
		<dl class="needs">
			<div><dt>Zotero 10 or later</dt><dd>Running, with "Allow other applications on this computer to communicate with Zotero" on.</dd></div>
			<div><dt>An account with a model provider</dt><dd>Any provider that pi supports, or a local model. See <a href="/models/">Models</a> for the tested ones.</dd></div>
			<div><dt>A folder for notes</dt><dd>Plain Markdown files. An Obsidian vault works.</dd></div>
		</dl>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section">
	<div class="wrap split">
		<div>
			<p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
			<h2>Your library stays in Zotero.</h2>
		</div>
		<div class="prose-block">
			<p>Sub-Sub talks to Zotero through its local API and never uses your zotero.org account. It sends no usage data.</p>
			<p>The model provider that you choose receives your messages and what the tools return: titles, authors, abstracts, and parts of a full text when you ask for a note. PubMed, Europe PMC, OpenAlex, Crossref and Unpaywall receive search terms and identifiers, not your notes.</p>
			<p><a href="/privacy/">What goes where</a></p>
		</div>
	</div>
</section>

